# Personal edition: leave these off. Ask the soul inside Claude Code with /soul; it runs on your
# Claude subscription. The dashboard's ask box then answers offline from the inventory and stats.
# Community edition: turn the ask box on to answer through the Anthropic API (billed per token).
# SOUL_ASK_API=on
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides
# SOUL_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# SOUL_EFFORT=low
# SOUL_PORT=7777
# SOUL_DAYS=30
# SOUL_DEMO=1
# Project inventory (INVENTORY button, /find in the terminal)
# Folders whose sub-folders are projects to scan, besides the ones Claude Code worked in (; or , separated)
# SOUL_INVENTORY_ROOTS=C:/Users/you/Dev
# Your own domains: addresses on them are shown in full; personal and client addresses are masked
# SOUL_OWN_DOMAINS=example.com
# Folders to leave out (a regular expression on the full path)
# SOUL_INVENTORY_EXCLUDE=archive|old-
# The REKA continuity check script the core may run (a repo's own tools/reka-handover-kit copy wins)
# SOUL_CONTINUITY_CHECK=/path/to/continuity-check.js
# Where daily inventory snapshots are kept for the change report (default ~/.claude/soul-engine/inventory-history)
# SOUL_DATA_DIR=
